Exercise: sa-proc-review (chapter 8 lab)

Work on servera, with sudo or as root.

Processes (all as the user "worker", who you create first)
 1. Start "sleep 7000" in the background so that it survives a closed
    terminal, with a niceness of 5.
 2. Start "sleep 7001" in the background and change its niceness to 12.
    Then pause it (stop it, do not kill it).
 3. Start "sleep 7002" in the background, then terminate it with the
    default (polite) signal. It must not be running when you grade.

Tuning
 4. Install the tuned package, enable and start the tuned service, and
    select the profile throughput-performance.

On workstation
 5. Fill in the four signal numbers in answers.txt.

Then, on workstation:  lab grade sa-proc-review
